{"32":[{"k":"p","t":"MOVING THE MACHINE"},{"k":"p","t":"This machine is fitted with castors to make it easier to move. Take care when moving the machine on an inclined surface."},{"k":"p","t":"The overall height of the machine is 2280mm. Take care of any overhead obstructions. (e.g. Light Fittings, Electric Cables etc.)"},{"k":"p","t":"INSTALLATION"},{"k":"p","t":"Notes on Installation"},{"k":"tr","t":"WARNING   +   NEVER turn the power to the machine ON until"},{"k":"p","t":"installation has been completed."},{"k":"tr","t":"WARNING   -   In order to prevent possible electric shocks, be sure"},{"k":"p","t":"that the machine is connected to the mains with a securely connected earthed plug."},{"k":"tr","t":"WARNING   +   So that customers are not injured , ensure that there is"},{"k":"p","t":"at least 500mm separation between other machines or walls."},{"k":"tr","t":"CAUTION   -   In order to avoid damage to the machine due to mis-"},{"k":"p","t":"operation, ensure that the voltage of the mains supply is 230volts AC."},{"k":"h","t":"NOTE . If the location site of this machine has a polished floor it is"},{"k":"p","t":"recommended that rubber pads are fitted under the level adjusters to prevent the machine sliding on the floor."},{"k":"p","t":"> In order to gain access to the Power Supply and CPU assemblies, make sure that the rear of the machine is separated from a wall or other machine by at least 500mm."},{"k":"p","t":". When installation is complete, it is imperative that the game is initialized. (See section 7 page 54)"}],"44":[{"k":"p","t":"6-2 Adjustment Switches"},{"k":"p","t":"The Adjustment switches are located inside the coin door."},{"k":"p","t":"1. Service Switch. Press this switch to obtain game credits without incrementing the play meter."},{"k":"p","t":"Test Switch Slide the test switch ON to enter test mode. Test mode allows testing and the changing of game settings. (Refer to section 6-3 \"Test Mode\" page 45)"},{"k":"p","t":"Select Up/Down Switch This switch is used to select the test required when in the Test Mode."},{"k":"p","t":"Enter Switch This switch is used to enter a selected test and to change settings within a test."},{"k":"p","t":"COIN COUNTER"},{"k":"p","t":"2 Amp Q/B (Coin Fuse) \u00b0 fe)"},{"k":"p","t":"PLAYER 1 PLAYER 2"},{"k":"p","t":"UP UP @| SELECT @| SELECT DOWN DOWN"},{"k":"p","t":"SELECT SELECT"},{"k":"tr","t":"O   \u201c\u00a9   O   \u201coe"},{"k":"tr","t":"TEST   SERVICE   TEST   SERVICE"},{"k":"tr","t":"\u00a9   t   )"}],"48":[{"k":"h","t":"ITEM DESCRIPTION FACTORY SET"},{"k":"tr","t":"(a) PCB ID   Sets PCB number to player number ---- settable 1 - 4   1/2"},{"k":"tr","t":"(b) Horse Type   Sets horse family name ---- settable 1-4   1/2"},{"k":"h","t":"(c) Difficulty Sets game play difficulty EASY - NORMAL - HARD NORMAL"},{"k":"tr","t":"(d) Broadcast   Commentary during race ---- On/Off   ON"},{"k":"li","t":"(e) Sound in Attract |Set if sound played in attract mode ON /OFF ON"},{"k":"tr","t":"(f) Main Race   Length game will select. - 1200m 1600m 2400m   1600m"},{"k":"tr","t":"(g) Auto Select   Horse selectected by game not player   OFF"},{"k":"tr","t":"(h) Gate Setting   Starting Gate Number - RANDOM, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8   RANDOM"},{"k":"tr","t":"(i) Record Keep   Stores race times at power off   ON"},{"k":"tr","t":"(j) Result Keep   Stores race results at power off   ON"},{"k":"li","t":"(k) Record Initialize"},{"k":"p","t":"(I) Result Initialize"},{"k":"note","t":"Note:"},{"k":"p","t":"() PCB ID numbers are assigned so that they are not duplicated on the linked seats. Be sure to set these correctly to avoid link absence or other operation faults. PCB ID numbers (1 ~ 4) are linked to the numbers of the current players (1P ~ 4P)."},{"k":"p","t":"(ii) Each seat is assigned a horse family name. Be careful not to duplicate family names in linked seats. The machine will not operate correctly if the settings are incorrect. The family names are numbered as follows:"},{"k":"p","t":"1 - Funky 2 - Magic Cert 4- Sky"},{"k":"p","t":"(iii) The same degree of difficulty must be set for all of the linked seats. If different degrees of difficulty are set, the machine will not operate correctly."}],"50":[{"k":"p","t":"6-3-3-1 Switch Test"},{"k":"li","t":"1. Select \u201cSwitch Test\u201d on the I/O menu screen to test the switches. The following screen is displayed."},{"k":"li","t":"2. The display shows the current state of the switches."},{"k":"li","t":"3. Press the Up Select switch and the Enter switch together to EXIT and return to the I/O menu screen"},{"k":"p","t":"(i)"},{"k":"p","t":"(ii) to (vii)"},{"k":"p","t":"(viii)"},{"k":"p","t":"(ix)"},{"k":"note","t":"Note: ( SWITCH TEST >)"},{"k":"tr","t":"TEST SW   ON   (i)"},{"k":"tr","t":"SERVICE SW   OFF.   (ii)"},{"k":"tr","t":"UP SELECT SW   OFF.   (ii)"},{"k":"tr","t":"DOWN SELECT Sw   OFF.   (iv)"},{"k":"tr","t":"ENTER SW   OFF .   (v)"},{"k":"tr","t":"LEFT STICK (WHIP) SW   OFF.   (vi)"},{"k":"tr","t":"RIGHT STICK (WHIP) SW   OOF...   (vii)"},{"k":"p","t":"HANDLE * * * * CENTER (viii) SWING **** CENTER (ix)"},{"k":"p","t":"\\.__UP SELECT SW + ENTER SW : EXIT _/"},{"k":"p","t":"If the test switch is turned OFF during this test, the game will return to normal game mode."},{"k":"p","t":"The display will change from OFF to ON as each switch is operated."},{"k":"p","t":"When the head is turned to the left, the numbers (\u00ab*++) change and the display will change from CENTER to LEFT OK. When the head is turned to the right, the numbers (****) change and the display will change from CENTER to RIGHT OK."},{"k":"p","t":"When the horse is rocked fully backwards and forwards, the numbers (**\u00ab*) will change and OK will be displayed for both front and back movement."},{"k":"p","t":"If OK is not displayed for items (viii) or (ix) first re-initialize the game, (See section 7), before checking or replacing the control pot."}],"68":[{"k":"p","t":"10.PARTS"},{"k":"p","t":"9or ll"},{"k":"p","t":"Item Description Pa